WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.160
On the final day of the inaugural concert,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.190
they plan to celebrate the fifth 
anniversary of Re:vale's formation.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.530
They'd like us to perform 
as a surprise guest.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.170
We're thinking of singing 
"Dis one." as our last song.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.680
You mean Zero's big hit?

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.990
You're Osaka Sogo-san of MEZZO", aren't you?

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.870
Wait, are you Aya-chan?

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.950
Don't you feel like Mitsuki 
gets in the way, though?

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.790
He's not even popular.
I wish he'd read the room.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.120
Tenn-nii, it hurts.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.000
Being irreplaceable and 
being replaceable both hurt...

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.800
Mitsuki, did something happen?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.610
No.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.280
You're lying! Your eyes are red.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.610
Look. Your eyes look just like Kinako's.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.730
It's nothing.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:04.330
I got shampoo in my eyes and have been 
rubbing them too much because of my hay fever.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.330
But...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.710
Just leave me alone!

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.880
Oh...

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.360
You don't need to worry about me.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.320
I'm fine.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:19.970
Mitsuki...

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.520
Discover...

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.740
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.810
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.150
Wow...

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:50.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:55.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.530
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:06.250
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.930
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.470
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.880
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.430
Discover...

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:27.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.240
Night sky

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.110
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.580
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:41.160
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.450
Wow...

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.030
#07 Discord Bleeding Through

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.510
Good morning, Nanase-san.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.660
G-Good morning, Iori...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.170
<b>Kinako</b>

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.410
Good morning.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.250
Good morning.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.670
Congratulations.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:19.080
Your new song is your best selling song yet.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.930
I'll tell the president. We should celebrate.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.940
Really? That's great.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.030
Nanase-san...

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.650
I'm gonna check the schedule.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.690
I wonder what's wrong with Riku-kun.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.650
What is with him, anyway?!

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.230
You surprised me.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.940
I expected this from the start.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.360
I knew we'd be compared.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.330
He even smiled and thanked me...

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.650
That traitor.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.950
Iori-kun, are you okay?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.040
I don't know.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.410
Iori-kun...

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:54.390
Who do you think wanted you to sing the most?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.540
<b>Lovely Night With You! Segment Planning</b>

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:00.210
Anyway, Riku-san and Iori-san will 
be attending this on-location shoot.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.030
What?

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.420
Nanase-san's health is in poor condition.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.160
I believe Rokuya-san and I should go instead.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:11.620
Oh?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.180
What?

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:13.990
Which is it?

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.200
Um...

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.610
Then let's do the following.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.800
Ichi and Nagi go to the shoot.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.160
MEZZO" is busy, so Mitsu and the guest can...

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.360
Mitsu, are you listening?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.950
Yeah, I'm listening. I'm good.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.080
Yamato, Mitsuki is feeling down.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.690
I'll interact with the guest.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.560
Sounds like quite the entanglement.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.500
Mitsu, are you okay with that?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.530
Yeah.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:46.470
Riku-san and Iori-san,
are you all right with that?

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.010
Yes.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.020
Don't worry about what people are saying.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.150
We just have to do the best 
we can with what we've got.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.270
Okay...

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.770
Okay.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:15.790
I'll set a Perfection Gimmick on 
you, I want you to feel Amazing

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:23.210
I want to show you Another face 
more grown up than my usual self

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:30.640
Perfection Gimmick, we are 
Jugglers sparkling in the night

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:37.140
I'll lure you in with a yet unknown
and special spell I'll be

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.120
Drawing the delight. It's wonder night…

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.210
We are IDOLiSH7!

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.180
Thank you!

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.440
Iorin!

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.170
Iori-kun, you're the best!

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.170
Iorin was awesome!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.670
I hope he stays the center forever!

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.130
I know what you mean!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.320
And their new CD is selling better than ever.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:10.980
Yeah!

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:16.290
Since IDOLiSH7 is getting popular, it makes 
sense that their sales are increasing.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.000
Iori's fans are so rude, aren't they?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.770
They want him to keep being the center 
even though Rikkun's a good singer.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.350
What's with them? Gross.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.900
I bet they're jealous.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.020
They're panicking because Iori-kun 
is becoming more popular.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.400
I bet that's it.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:36.540
What? Hey, we can hear you, y'know.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.100
Oh, yeah? We could say the same thing.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:39.920
What?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.720
What?

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.050
Y'know, I've always thought...

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.050
Don't fight, guys.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.710
I hate this.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.720
<b>Re:vale to perform cover of Zero's 
"Dis one." at arena's inaugural concert!</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.720
Re:vale announced that they're 
covering Zero's song.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.700
Zero still has a lot of passionate fans.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.980
I bet the response is insane.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.850
So, what do you think of the cover?

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.010
It's awful.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.730
What? Have you always hated Zero that much?

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.390
What? Oh, sorry.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:11.990
Riku-kun and Iori-kun's fans 
are arguing on social media.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.220
Arguing?

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:18.000
About who's more popular and 
who's the better center.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.960
<b>Will Silently Follow Iori Fans
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Please keep Iori-kun as the center forever
。。。
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Iori is a better center than Riku
</b>

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:23.250
Some fans were arguing after 
our concert the other day.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.250
<b>Ainana 7 Oshi
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Iori is just subbing in
Hoping for Center Riku
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Riku, come back</b>

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.840
And perhaps because of that, Ichi and 
Riku have been acting strange, too.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.080
I see.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.650
What is it? Have people been 
saying stuff about you, too?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:32.380
No.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:36.810
I'm fairly innocuous,
so I don't get a lot of hate.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.670
But it reminded me of the past.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.150
The past?

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.580
Of my uncle.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.400
Whenever his name came up among 
family, he was disavowed.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.530
<b>Osaka Family</b>

00:07:55.450 --> 00:08:03.960
<b>Ainana 7 Oshi
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Iori is just subbing in
Hoping for Center Riku
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Riku, come back
Ai7 Cheer Squad
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Could you guys not ruin the official account's replies...
Ioriii!
@[Official] IDOLiSH7-san,
Don't forget that their single is selling well because of Iori-kun</b>

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.740
Someone I cared about was rejected,

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.320
and despite my best efforts, 
I couldn't defend him.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.960
Remembering my past was a little painful.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:08.460
I wish there were something I could 
do for Riku-kun and Iori-kun.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.210
It'll be okay.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.840
You should work on deepening your 
friendship with your partner.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.890
It's plenty deep already.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.900
I think we've reached our max.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.060
You make it sound like 
you've figured it all out.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.760
It's true. We're complete opposites.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.560
I don't think there's anything 
we can do about it at this point.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.030
The other day, after recording...

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.170
That girl...

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.770
Oh! Never mind. It's nothing.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.880
Mitsuki-san has been down recently, too.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:54.640
Mitsu's always the guy who lights 
up the group at times like these.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:59.140
Even Nagi the optimist seems down 
because he's worried about him.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.640
I wonder what happened.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.290
He's gotten more jobs on variety shows and 
even recognition from older personalities.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:09.650
Mitsu wants recognition from our fans, 
not from people in the industry.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.810
I'm sure the fans recognize him.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.980
I'm not.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:18.280
Unlike with singing and dancing, 
it's hard to convey MC skills.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:18.910
Huh?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.310
An MC is like a spotlight.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:27.910
They keep the light on guys who look 
good and off guys who look tired.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:31.020
While making snap decisions,

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.810
they manage the conversation so 
everyone gets equal time in the light.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.950
It's an incredible job.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.950
I could never do it.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.450
It is amazing.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:44.850
But when you look at the stage, it's not 
the spotlight that draws your attention.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.190
It's the people <i>in </i>the spotlight.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:52.470
Fans that want to see their favorite 
in the light are bound to complain.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:56.300
Yamato-san, you should 
tell this to Mitsuki-san.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.690
I'm sure it would cheer him up.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.440
About that...

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:01.290
Is there a problem?

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.750
He's way prouder than we think.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.090
Proud?

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:11.030
So is Tama. You should be careful.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:12.310
What about you?

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:14.990
I vary a lot depending on the day.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:17.510
That's the hardest type to deal with.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.450
There you are.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.010
So-chan, the manager's calling you.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.330
Thanks.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.640
Excuse me, Yamato-san.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.770
Later.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.610
By the way, Tamaki-kun, could you show me 
a picture of your sister if you've got one?

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.610
Sorry. I don't have one.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.720
If I did, I'd have already shown you.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.100
I see. Thank you.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.220
Sure.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.850
Hey, Tama.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.460
Let's get ramen.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.540
Come with me.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.770
You're paying? All right!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.880
<b>Ramen  Nana House</b>

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:58.170
One miso chashu pork ramen 
and one shoyu ramen.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.420
This looks so good.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.710
Thanks for the food.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:04.890
Eat up.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:10.890
<b>Ichimi Togarashi</b>

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.230
Why ramen all of a sudden?

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.890
I wanted to talk to you about So.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.520
About So-chan?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.400
I was talking to him earlier. And...

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.740
He's a huge fan of yours.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.220
Okay, you're lying.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.700
I'm not lying.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.670
He respects your talents as a dancer.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.870
He even said he looks up to you.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:37.190
So he ends up being hard on you 
because he wants you to look good.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.460
What? So-chan said that? Really?

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:46.050
Yeah. I was all, "You should 
tell him that yourself, then."

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.100
But he's shy, y'know?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:52.500
He looked flustered when he said 
he was too embarrassed to tell you.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:53.620
Huh...

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:58.370
So even if he's a little 
hard on you, don't get mad.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.450
It's just because he expects so much of you.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:04.430
He really, <i>really</i> loves you.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.890
I see. So that's how it is.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.610
He should just say so.

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:10.580
Right?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:18.090
<b>Beer 
</b>We have it!

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.890
Should we bring back some 
gyoza for So-chan?

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.080
Yeah.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.170
<i>No hard feelings, Tama.</i>

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.660
<i>Riku and Ichi are fighting, 
Mitsu is depressed,</i>

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.680
<i>and he's dragging Nagi down with him.</i>

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:30.330
<i>If MEZZO" starts having problems, 
I'll be over capacity.</i>

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.520
Mister, more noodles.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.190
Got it.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.640
Feel free to get seconds, 
thirds, or seasoned eggs, too.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.290
If it'll make things go well, 
eat all the noodles you want.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.840
Yama-san, you're super nice.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:48.390
<b>Ramen  Nana House</b>

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.930
In that case, could I get more chashu?

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:55.500
Today's guest is MEZZO".

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:00.500
Yeah!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.510
<b>I love MEZZO"</b>

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.510
<b>I'm so in love!</b>

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.510
<b>MEZZO" fan</b>

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.010
Listen to those cheers.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.190
Thank you.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.510
How have you been? Getting along?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.250
I supp—

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.900
We're getting along great.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.100
We're best buds—I mean, friends.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.620
Well, aren't you excited.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.930
Are you guys really that close?

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.980
Yeah—I mean, yes.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:25.450
Sometimes So-chan gets mad at me, but 
Yama-san said that's how he cares for me.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.450
Yama-san? You mean Nikaido Yamato-kun?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:32.890
Yeah. He drinks beer all the time, but 
sometimes he says some smart things.

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:36.250
I see. Why don't you show 
us how close you are, then?

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.460
How close?

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:38.500
Sure.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:40.970
This close.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.410
Are you guys all right?

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.630
Won't you lose your voices?

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:50.010
Shh, quiet. Be quiet while we're talking.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.330
I told you to shh.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.520
Be quiet, shh.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:57.020
Good work today.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:58.630
Thank you.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.390
I look forward to working with you again.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.790
I-I look forward to working with you again.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.570
Thank you.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.650
Tamaki-kun?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:08.560
How polite of you, Tamaki-kun.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.640
Is Sogo-kun's training paying off?

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.090
See you guys later.

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:14.060
See you later.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.810
What's gotten into you, Tamaki-kun?

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:20.040
What? Was that strange?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.200
It wasn't strange.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.690
Didn't you hear him? He praised you.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.280
He said you were polite.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:27.700
Does it make you happy when people praise me?

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.640
Yeah. Personally, I find it hugely rewarding!

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.730
You gently scolded the audience 
during recording, too.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:36.490
You were awesome.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.860
Oh, right. Thanks for asking 
about my sister the other day.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.620
Ah, sure...

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.970
So-chan, you're so nice.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.650
Am I?

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:52.000
I'll forgive you for the pudding.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.390
Really? I'm sorry. Thank—

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.920
Hey, don't we have the 
same day off next month?

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.660
Huh? Y-Yeah.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.170
Want to go somewhere together?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:06.180
What? Wh-Where is this 
coming from, Tamaki-kun?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.830
Did you eat something bad—

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:12.670
<i>No, Tamaki-kun is reaching out 
to me. Why am I doubting him?</i>

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.720
<i>Stop being childish, me!</i>

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.680
Sure, Tamaki-kun.
Let's go someplace together.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.530
All right! It's a promise.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.480
Yeah.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.740
Let's pick up some King 
Pudding on the way home.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:25.080
All right!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.850
<i>It was worth the effort.</i>

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:31.490
King Pudding!

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.490
<b>Lovely Night With You!</b>

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.280
We're ready to start.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:42.830
Okay.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.930
<i>I'll try not to talk too much.</i>

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.720
<i>I'll say only what I need 
to say to make the fans happy.</i>

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.000
<i>I should be able to do it.</i>

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.730
<i>If I can't, then there's no 
reason for me to be here.</i>

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.640
We're starting in three, two...

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:09.730
<i>Lovely Night With You!</i>

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.740
Yeah!

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:13.960
Good evening, everyone.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:18.640
Today we'd like to jump right into 
our cherry blossom viewing special.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:22.060
So, Riku, do you have any memories 
related to flower viewing?

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.620
What? Flower viewing?

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.720
I've never gone flower viewing.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.400
What? Seriously?

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.140
Yeah.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.730
<i>Riku seems down.</i>

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.600
<i>Is it all right if I stay on this subject?</i>

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.740
<i>Would that give me too much screen time?</i>

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:39.660
Really? In that case,
let's go together sometime.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.060
How do you want to do it?

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.390
What? Well...

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.280
I'd like to see the cherry blossoms at night.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.860
I want to try securing a spot, too.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.020
Nobody says they want to secure a spot.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.610
Really?

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:53.680
So cute!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.610
<i>Uh-oh. Am I talking too much?</i>

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.850
<i>I wish everyone would talk more.</i>

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.870
<i>Iori's right next to him. He should butt in.</i>

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:03.320
Iori, any flower viewing memories?

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:06.020
We went as a family when we were little.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.680
<i>Don't end the conversation immediately.</i>

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.620
<i>Keep talking.</i>

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.380
I guess we did. What was it like?

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.430
You don't remember, Nii-san?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.930
<b>Lovely Night With You!</b>

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.930
<i>I do remember, but I can't 
be the one to talk about it.</i>

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:24.820
Of course I remember.

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.190
<i>What do the fans want to see?</i>

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.940
<i>What do they want to hear?</i>

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:33.190
Let's head into our first segment.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:37.850
<i>What can I do here to be useful to the group?</i>

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.200
<b>Mitsuki</b>

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.040
Sogo's Magical Cooking.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.900
What's he cooking in his magical pot today?

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:47.460
Thank you.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.710
Thanks.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.890
What was wrong with Mitsuki-kun today?

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:52.870
He seemed a little off.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:57.400
The other members don't talk 
much if he's not on his game.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.670
I hope he's back to normal 
by the next episode.

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:08.350
Mitsuki, wait!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.530
We need to talk. It's important.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.640
What? Is it about Cocona?

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.360
It's about you.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.910
I told you, I'm fine. Later!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:20.870
Mitsuki!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.450
I caught you!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.370
Damn it! Let go!

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:25.810
Don't fight it.

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.620
Shall we talk like this?

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.380
No!

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:34.510
Then let's speak face to face.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.210
Oh!

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.350
Please don't run.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:42.140
Mitsuki, it makes me sad 
when you run from me.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.100
Do you hate me?

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.140
That's not it...

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:49.710
Tell me.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.930
Sorry about today.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.560
I didn't manage the conversation very well.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.070
I'll do better next time.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:06.690
I'll do better... I promise I'll do better.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:13.690
But... I'm not sure how
 I'm <i>supposed</i> to do better.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.540
You don't need to try so hard.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:19.770
Mitsuki, when you're feeling down, 
you don't need to try so hard.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.370
You can just be yourself.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.350
What's wrong with that?

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:26.700
But I...

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:30.350
Can I be pathetic for a second?

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.470
As much as you need.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:37.070
I...

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.840
I don't want to be disliked.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:50.290
I don't need everyone 
in the world to like me.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:55.370
I just don't want the people who 
love you guys to hate me.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.750
Mitsuki...

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.110
I want them to be happy, Nagi.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:06.510
I want <i>everyone</i> to be happy!

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:11.720
Riku has his singing, Tamaki has his 
dancing, and you've got your looks...

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:14.190
I want to make people happy with me.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:19.210
Hey, Nagi. What should I do?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:25.120
Is it okay for me to be a part of IDOLiSH7?

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.310
What are you talking about?

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:33.060
Without you, we wouldn't be IDOLiSH7.

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:39.510
Don't cry, Mitsuki.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:42.750
Who made you this sad?

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.720
Who could be so cruel?

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:48.430
No one. It wasn't anyone, Nagi.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.780
What is my role?

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:54.440
What can I do?

00:20:54.810 --> 00:21:02.010
How should I respond to the affection 
of all the people in the city?

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.370
I just want them to be happy...

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:15.670
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:21.880
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:34.270
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:40.480
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:46.230
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.610
The sound of the future

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:52.810
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:56.040
We quietly adorn

00:21:56.040 --> 00:22:01.800
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:05.190
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:09.690
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:14.930
So I always want you by my side

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:45.830
I don't like IDOLiSH7 these days.

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:49.340
There are fans who are mean to Mitsuki-kun.

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:51.470
He's trying so hard, too.

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:55.960
Same. Some people are saying 
they don't need Rikkun.

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:59.940
I hope Rikkun hasn't heard 
what they're saying.

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:02.090
Me, too.

00:23:02.890 --> 00:23:08.490
Both Rikkun and Iori-kun are cool, but 
the moment Iori-kun became the center,

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:10.820
everyone started trash-talking
 one or the other.

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:12.640
It's awful.

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:16.540
<i>The new Zero Arena's inaugural performance!</i>

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:16.540
That's Zero's song.

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:19.500
Re:vale's covering it, right?

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:22.790
It's gonna be so cool!

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.810
They're singing it at Zero Arena's 
inaugural concert, right?

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.970
The inaugural concert has an amazing lineup.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.120
Re:vale, TRIGGER, and...

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:32.800
IDOLiSH7!

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.520
They were awesome at <i>Black or White</i>, too.

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:44.190
That's when I decided 
to become a serious fan.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:47.070
I definitely want to see 
the inaugural concert.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:48.600
I'm so hyped!

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:50.570
The posters are so cool, too!

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:52.010
Oh, look!

00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:58.770
What's that?

00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"I Want You to Know!"</b>
